<section id="privacy-viz">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div style="text-align:center;max-width:600px;margin:0 auto;">
      <span class="eyebrow rev">Privacy architecture</span>
      <h2 class="sh rev d1">See exactly where<br>your data <em>doesn't go</em></h2>
      <p class="sb rev d2" style="margin:0 auto;">Most document apps route your files through external servers. Zari Vault is architecturally different.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pv-grid">
      <div class="rev-l">
        <div class="pv-diagram">
          <div style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
            <span class="pv-section-label good">✓ Zari Vault: your data flow</span>
            <div class="pv-row">
              <div class="pv-node phone">📱</div>
              <div class="pv-arrow good"><span class="pv-arrow-label">AES-256 encrypt</span></div>
              <div class="pv-node enc">🔐</div>
              <div class="pv-arrow good"><span class="pv-arrow-label">stored locally</span></div>
              <div class="pv-node vault">🏠</div>
            </div>
            <div style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--text-2);margin-top:.5rem;">Your phone → Encrypted → Stays on your device. Full stop.</div>
          </div>
          <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding-top:1.5rem;">
            <span class="pv-section-label bad">✗ Typical cloud document app</span>
            <div class="pv-row">
              <div class="pv-node phone">📱</div>
              <div class="pv-arrow bad"><span class="pv-arrow-label">upload</span></div>
              <div class="pv-node server">🖥️</div>
              <div class="pv-arrow bad"><span class="pv-arrow-label">sync / share</span></div>
              <div class="pv-node cloud">☁️</div>
            </div>
            <div class="pv-blocked">⚠️ Breach risk · Subpoena risk · Third-party sharing</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="pv-facts rev-r">
        <div class="pv-fact">
          <div class="pv-fact-label">The reality</div>
          <h3>Your ID number unlocks your entire life</h3>
          <p>Bank accounts, credit, SIM registration, property. Once an ID number leaks, fraudsters use it for years, opening accounts and taking loans in your name long after the breach.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pv-fact">
          <div class="pv-fact-label">Cloud risk</div>
          <h3>Every server upload is a potential breach</h3>
          <p>When your documents live on a server, they're exposed to insider threats, hackers, and government orders, regardless of what a privacy policy says. No server means no breach surface.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pv-fact">
          <div class="pv-fact-label">Your POPIA rights</div>
          <h3>South Africans have strong data protections</h3>
          <p>Under POPIA, you have the right to know what data is collected about you, to access it, correct it, or delete it. Any app storing your documents is a data processor, and must notify you of breaches.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ABOUT -->
<section id="about">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow rev">Our Story</span>
    <h2 class="sh rev d1">We built the app we <em>needed</em> ourselves</h2>
    <div class="ab-grid">
      <div class="ab-vis rev-l">
        <div class="ab-vis-icon">🔐</div>
        <h3>Privacy isn't a feature. It's the foundation.</h3>
        <p>Most document apps upload your most sensitive information to servers owned by companies you've never heard of. We built Zari Vault to be architecturally different. Your documents never leave your device because our infrastructure literally cannot receive them.</p>
        <div class="ab-vis-stats">
          <div class="ab-stat"><div class="ab-stat-n">0</div><div class="ab-stat-l">Servers storing your data</div></div>
          <div class="ab-stat"><div class="ab-stat-n">149</div><div class="ab-stat-l">Countries supported</div></div>
          <div class="ab-stat"><div class="ab-stat-n">AES‑256</div><div class="ab-stat-l">Encryption standard</div></div>
          <div class="ab-stat"><div class="ab-stat-n">3s</div><div class="ab-stat-l">Average access time</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="rev-r">
        <div class="ab-body">
          <p>Zari Vault was born from a simple frustration: fumbling through a wallet at an estate boom gate, failing to find an expired licence at a roadblock, scrambling for a passport number during online check-in.</p>
          <p>We designed Zari Vault to feel like the app that actually lives on your home screen. Fast, clean, and completely private. No account to create, no email to verify, no data to hand over.</p>
          <p>POPIA compliant by architecture, not by checkbox. South Africa's data protection law demands better from every app that handles your personal information. Zari Vault was built to exceed that standard.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ab-vals">
          <div class="ab-val rev d1"><div class="ab-val-i">🏠</div><div><h4>Privacy by architecture</h4><p>We can't access your data because our system is built to never receive it. That's not a promise. It's a technical fact.</p></div></div>
          <div class="ab-val rev d2"><div class="ab-val-i">⚡</div><div><h4>Speed in the real world</h4><p>Every UI decision is made with one question: can you show your document before the security guard loses patience?</p></div></div>
          <div class="ab-val rev d3"><div class="ab-val-i">🇿🇦</div><div><h4>Built for Africa, used everywhere</h4><p>Boom gates, roadblocks, FICA compliance, designed around real South African daily friction, with global reach.</p></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <!-- Founder's Note -->
    <div class="rev" style="background:#0f2460;border-radius:var(--r-xl);padding:2.5rem 2.75rem;margin-bottom:4rem;position:relative;overflow:hidden;">
      <div style="position:absolute;top:-40px;right:-40px;width:180px;height:180px;background:rgba(234,88,12,.1);border-radius:50%;pointer-events:none;"></div>
      <div style="position:absolute;bottom:-60px;left:-30px;width:200px;height:200px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.03);border-radius:50%;pointer-events:none;"></div>
      <span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:.4rem;background:rgba(234,88,12,.2);border:1px solid rgba(234,88,12,.35);color:#fdba74;font-size:.72rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;padding:.3rem .85rem;border-radius:100px;margin-bottom:1.25rem;position:relative;">✍️ Founder's Note</span>
      <h3 style="font-size:1.5rem;font-weight:800;color:#fff;letter-spacing:-.02em;margin-bottom:1.5rem;position:relative;">Why I built Zari Vault</h3>
      <div style="position:relative;">
        <p style="font-size:.97rem;color:rgba(255,255,255,.82);line-height:1.85;margin-bottom:1rem;">I built Zari Vault after I was mugged and lost my ID and driver's licence. What frustrated me most wasn't the loss, it was everything that came after: the slow process, the cost, the realisation that there was no reliable way to show my own documents without risking the physical originals all over again. I kept asking why this didn't already exist. Eventually I decided the solution to my problem was going to have to come from me.</p>
        <p style="font-size:.97rem;color:rgba(255,255,255,.82);line-height:1.85;margin-bottom:1rem;">So I built it myself, from scratch.</p>
        <p style="font-size:.97rem;color:rgba(255,255,255,.82);line-height:1.85;margin-bottom:1rem;">The privacy part isn't a marketing angle for me, it's the whole point. Right now almost every company treats your personal information as a product to be sold, and you don't really get a say. If you don't hand your data over, you get left behind. I didn't want to build another company like that. I don't want to own anyone's information. I don't want ads on this platform. I don't want a quick payday. I wanted to solve a real problem I actually had, and it turns out I'm far from the only person who has it.</p>
        <p style="font-size:.97rem;color:rgba(255,255,255,.82);line-height:1.85;margin-bottom:1.75rem;">That's Zari Vault. Your documents, on your device, controlled by you. Nothing leaves your phone, because I built it so that it can't.</p>
        <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.85rem;">
          <div style="width:44px;height:44px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.12);border-radius:50%;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:.9rem;font-weight:800;color:#fff;flex-shrink:0;">MM</div>
          <div>
            <p style="font-size:.88rem;font-weight:700;color:#fff;margin:0;">Miense Mpasa</p>
            <p style="font-size:.75rem;color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);margin:0;">Founder &amp; CEO, Zari Vault</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="team-hdr"><span class="eyebrow rev">The Team</span><h2 class="sh rev d1" style="margin-top:.5rem;">The people behind <em>your vault</em></h2></div>
    <div class="team-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:2rem;max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">

      <!-- Miense Mpasa -->
      <div class="tc rev d1" style="text-align:left;padding:2rem 2rem 1.75rem;display:flex;flex-direction:column;">
        <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:1rem;margin-bottom:1.25rem;">
          <div style="width:56px;height:56px;background:#1e3a8a;border-radius:50%;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:1rem;font-weight:800;color:#fff;flex-shrink:0;">MM</div>
          <div>
            <h3 style="font-size:1.05rem;margin-bottom:2px;">Miense Mpasa</h3>
            <div class="role">Founder &amp; CEO</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p style="font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:.85rem;">Miense Mpasa is from Pretoria, Gauteng, and now builds out of Centurion. He did not set out to start a tech company. He set out to solve a problem that made him furious.</p>
        <p style="font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:.85rem;">At 24, he was mugged and lost his ID and driver's licence. The loss itself was manageable. What followed was not: the slow process, the cost, and the realisation that there was no safe, private way to carry his own documents without putting the originals at risk again. One month later, he started building.</p>
        <p style="font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:.85rem;">Sound engineering graduate from the Academy of Sound Engineering, turned international sales executive across real estate, marketing, FMCG, law, and recruitment. Self-taught developer: CSS, HTML, JavaScript, Python. He codes the product himself, which means every privacy decision in Zari Vault was made by the same person who felt the original problem.</p>
        <p style="font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:.85rem;">The privacy position is not a brand angle. It is the premise. Zari Vault collects no document data, runs no ads, and has no mechanism to monetise user information, because it was designed from the start to make that impossible.</p>
        <p style="font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:.85rem;">Ask him what the hardest part of building this has been and he does not say fundraising or distribution. He says the self-doubt, learning on the go, and being a solo founder without a network to lean on.</p>
        <p style="font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.8;font-style:italic;color:var(--text-2);margin-top:auto;padding-top:.75rem;">Mutable. Relentless. Unfinished.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Katleho Mohlomi -->
      <div class="tc rev d2" style="text-align:left;padding:2rem 2rem 1.75rem;display:flex;flex-direction:column;">
        <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:1rem;margin-bottom:1.25rem;">
          <div style="width:56px;height:56px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#1e3a8a,#ea580c);border-radius:50%;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:1rem;font-weight:800;color:#fff;flex-shrink:0;">KM</div>
          <div>
            <h3 style="font-size:1.05rem;margin-bottom:2px;">Katleho Mohlomi</h3>
            <div class="role">VP of Business Development &nbsp;·&nbsp; joined at inception</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p style="font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:.85rem;">Born in Johannesburg, raised in Pretoria, and now based in Cape Town, Katleho Mohlomi is not the product of a business school or a corporate ladder. He is the product of a decision made at 18: to skip university entirely and build something instead. He attended Cornwall Hill College before matriculating at Pretoria Boys High School. The day most of his peers were filling out university applications, he was registering Khari Moh Holdings.</p>
        <p style="font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:.85rem;">His first real test came during COVID-19. While the world shut down, Katleho identified an opportunity, began selling masks, and entered radio interviews to talk about what he was doing and why. The money he made didn't go toward lifestyle. It went toward the financial markets he had been studying since age 14. That foundation became Millionaire Contracts: a sales optimisation firm with 31 active clients, helping businesses grow revenue and reach markets they never imagined accessible.</p>
        <p style="font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:.85rem;">With limited prior exposure to the American market, he partnered with a US private equity firm managing a pool fund of approximately $50 million. He figured it out. That experience gave him a first-hand understanding of how the world is interconnected through finance, and why thinking beyond your geography is not optional for serious builders.</p>
        <p style="font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:.85rem;">His conviction around data sovereignty is personal. As someone who has had his own data used against him, and who watched AI-driven exploitation make ordinary people increasingly vulnerable, Katleho understands viscerally why most people hate having their information harvested and sold for ad revenue. That shared frustration is part of why he joined Zari Vault at inception.</p>
        <p style="font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.8;font-style:italic;color:var(--text-2);margin-top:auto;padding-top:.75rem;">One in eight billion.</p>
