          <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">Your documents are protected by your biometrics and AES-256 encryption. Even if someone has your physical phone, they cannot access the vault without your face or fingerprint. The data is not recoverable without authentication, which protects you, but also means documents can't be remotely restored. We recommend keeping original physical documents safe as a backup.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
          <span class="faq-q-text">Is a digital copy legally accepted in South Africa?</span>
          <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">Zari Vault stores personal copies for reference, not certified legal copies. For most everyday uses (estate access, pharmacies, showing a roadblock officer your details for reference, providing your member number), a phone copy works perfectly. For formal legal or FICA purposes, you'll still need certified originals. Zari Vault labels all stored documents as "Personal Copy" to make this clear.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
          <span class="faq-q-text">Can Zari Vault see my documents?</span>
          <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">No, and this is not a promise, it's a technical impossibility. Documents are encrypted on your device before being stored, using keys that only your device holds. Nothing is ever transmitted to our servers because we have no servers that receive document data. We have designed the system so that even if we wanted to see your documents, we couldn't.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
          <span class="faq-q-text">How is this different from just taking a photo on my phone?</span>
          <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">Photos live in your camera roll, unencrypted, accessible to any app that requests photo permissions, and synced to iCloud or Google Photos automatically. Zari Vault stores documents in an encrypted vault, locked by biometrics, with an auto-close timer, and completely isolated from other apps and cloud services. It's a fundamentally different security model.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
          <span class="faq-q-text">What is the auto-lock timer and why does it matter?</span>
          <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">When you open a document to show someone, it shouldn't stay on screen indefinitely. The auto-lock timer (30 seconds to 2 minutes, configurable on Premium) closes the document automatically after a set time. This prevents someone from grabbing your unlocked phone after you've shown a document and scrolling through your vault.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
          <span class="faq-q-text">How does the free plan differ from Premium?</span>
          <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">The free plan stores up to 4 documents with full biometric lock and AES-256 encryption. The core security is identical. Premium (R249.99/year, less than R21/month) unlocks storage for up to 10 documents, expiry alerts, custom nicknames, pinch-to-zoom, configurable auto-lock, and biometric-verified clipboard copy. See the <a href="#pricing">pricing section</a> for a full comparison.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
          <span class="faq-q-text">Is Zari Vault POPIA compliant?</span>
          <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">Yes, and by architecture, not just policy. POPIA requires organisations to protect personal information and be transparent about its use. Because Zari Vault never collects, processes, or transmits your personal data to any external system, the compliance is structural. We don't need a privacy policy that covers data handling because there's no data handling to cover.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
          <span class="faq-q-text">Which countries and document types are supported?</span>
          <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">149 countries are supported, with document types adapted per country. Your Smart ID in South Africa becomes an Aadhaar Card in India, a National ID in Kenya, and a BRP in the UK. Supported document types include: Smart ID / National ID, Driver's Licence, Passport, Student Card, Vehicle Registration / Licence Disc, Proof of Residence, Medical Aid / Health Insurance Card, and Vehicle Insurance Certificate.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

